#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128954 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9ea7a5-3ec2-516c-a755-bc9c7346efeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a CDF Given the PMF"}] :question/id #uuid "7c79d956-2ed2-55e0-9c02-e3a0d05351ac" :question/math-academy-id "e-7379" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the probability mass function $f(y)$, shown in the table below, and the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$, compute $F(2)$.\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f(y)$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is the function $F(y)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(y) = P(Y \\leq y)\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(2) &= P(Y \\le 2) \\\\\n&= P(Y ∈ {1, 2}) \\\\\n&= P(Y = 1) + P(Y = 2) \\\\\n&= f(1) + f(2) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{8} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{8}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128955 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b5f0085-01ab-5d16-884e-49200bc7ac14" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Given the CDF"}] :question/id #uuid "cc51477f-39b4-58ce-b898-5920471aca1c" :question/math-academy-id "e-7381" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$ shown in the table below, compute $P\\left(2 \\leq Y < 5 \\right)$.\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $F(y)$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{6}$ | $1$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is the function $F(y)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(y) = P(Y \\leq y)\n$$\n\nTo compute the probability of a random variable $Y$ over an interval, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(a < X \\leq b) = F(b) - F(a)\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute\n\n$$\nP\\left(2 \\leq Y < 5 \\right)\n$$\n\nHowever, this interval is stated in the form\n\n$$\na \\leq Y < b\n$$\n\nnot\n\n$$\na < Y \\leq b\n$$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval\n\n$$\n2 \\leq Y < 5\n$$\n\nto the form\n\n$$\na < X \\leq b\n$$\n\nLooking at the given possible values of $Y$, we see that\n\n$$\n2 \\leq Y\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $1 < Y$, and $Y< 5$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\nY \\leq 4\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(2 \\le Y < 5) &= P(1 < Y \\le 4) \\\\\n&= F(4) - F(1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{4} - \\frac{1}{4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128956 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2bc3af7-207d-5f4f-9d8c-94f441ef1686" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Probability of an Event Given the CDF"}] :question/id #uuid "819f255d-8a30-5d32-b085-9f9d4ec078a5" :question/math-academy-id "e-7382" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X=5)$.\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ | $7$ | $9$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.15$ | $0.45$ | $0.50$ | $0.90$ | $1.0$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x)\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(5) &= P(X \\le 5) \\\\\n&= P(X ∈ {1, 3, 5}) \\\\\n&= P(X = 1) + P(X = 3) + P(X = 5) \\\\\n&= P(X ∈ {1, 3}) + P(X = 5) \\\\\n&= P(X \\le 3) + P(X = 5) \\\\\n&= F(3) + P(X = 5)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X = 5) &= F(5) - F(3) \\\\\n&= 0.50 - 0.45 \\\\\n&= 0.05\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128957 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "566f4fc1-ba4d-5433-9812-a3f5470e3d1e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Containing a Greater Than Symbol"}] :question/id #uuid "60caa0af-285d-5f8c-9add-dc6254c2e6b2" :question/math-academy-id "e-7414" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X \\gt 2)$.\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ | $0.8$ | $0.9$ | $1.0$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x)\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X > a) = 1 - P(X\\leq a) = 1-F(a)\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X > 2) &= 1 - P(X \\le 2) \\\\\n&= 1 - F(2) \\\\\n&= 1 - 0.6 \\\\\n&= 0.4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129816 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9ea7a5-3ec2-516c-a755-bc9c7346efeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a CDF Given the PMF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e974dcb-31dc-56cf-b84c-fe3235f6601d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128691} {:answer/id #uuid "92a11bb6-9e9b-561a-85fd-565316f5375f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128692} {:answer/id #uuid "a89abd00-d7c2-5f3a-ac96-3743852bd715" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128693} {:answer/id #uuid "c8c4d35b-b444-5443-8d84-5915bd6ef6c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128694} {:answer/id #uuid "1b3d3b1b-2afa-5b37-9021-05a20be73894" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b3d3b1b-2afa-5b37-9021-05a20be73894" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128695} :answer-field/id #uuid "b68f825b-8d1